  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"55\" data-end=\"273\"><strong data-start=\"55\" data-end=\"62\">P/S</strong> stands for <strong data-start=\"74\" data-end=\"94\">Peripheral Smear</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"100\" data-end=\"124\">P/S for Microfilaria</strong> is a test where a <strong data-start=\"143\" data-end=\"158\">blood smear</strong> is examined under a microscope to detect the presence of <strong data-start=\"216\" data-end=\"233\">microfilariae</strong>&mdash;the larval stage of filarial parasites.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Result</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Microfilaria Detected</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Positive</strong> for filarial infection. Confirms active parasitemia. Species identification can be attempted based on morphology.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Microfilaria Not Detected</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Negative</strong> for detectable parasites at the time of testing. But <strong>does not rule out filariasis</strong> due to periodicity or low parasite load. Repeat testing or other methods may be required.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"1120\" data-end=\"1153\"><strong data-start=\"1125\" data-end=\"1153\">Important Considerations</strong></p>\n<p data-start=\"1155\" data-end=\"1193\"><strong data-start=\"1162\" data-end=\"1193\">Timing of Sample Collection</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1194\" data-end=\"1397\">\n<li data-start=\"1194\" data-end=\"1343\">\n<p data-start=\"1196\" data-end=\"1343\"><strong data-start=\"1196\" data-end=\"1226\">W. bancrofti and B. malayi</strong> show <strong data-start=\"1232\" data-end=\"1257\">nocturnal periodicity</strong> &rarr; microfilariae are typically present in peripheral blood between <strong data-start=\"1324\" data-end=\"1342\">10 PM and 2 AM</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1344\" data-end=\"1397\">\n<p data-start=\"1346\" data-end=\"1397\">Collect blood during this window for highest yield.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
